OL,3,GNEWSAPlans to cut parking fees not
OL,4,Aenough - councillors
OL,5,
OL,6,FPlans to cut parking charges in York do
OL,7,Fnot go far enough to reverse the
OL,8,Feffects of previous hikes, councillors
OL,9,Fand traders have claimed.
OL,11,FThe city's council has proposed
OL,12,Freducing the cost of residents' parking
OL,13,Fpermits by a third, while discounts in
OL,14,Fcommunity areas would increase to 50%.
OL,16,FIf councillors approve the planned
OL,17,Fchanges to Minster Badge discounts on
OL,18,FWednesday, permits would cost #15
OL,19,Fannually, rather than #45 for two
OL,20,Fyears. The Mister Badge gives residents
OL,21,Fdiscounts on parking in council car
OL,22,Fparks and on-street parking bays.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
